.nh
.TH "PB-TUNNEL-RENAME" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-tunnel-rename - Rename a durable tunnel


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb tunnel rename <tunnel> <name> [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Rename a durable tunnel, selected by ID or current name. The name is only a label: the
tunnel's address, routes, connectors and access rules do not change. To change the address
itself, use pb tunnel address.

.PP
A change returns once the request is accepted, and the tunnel may still be connecting. Pass
--wait to wait (at most --timeout, default 2m, 1s to 10m) until it finishes, or check pb tunnel
status.

.PP
JSON output is supported with --json.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for rename

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print canonical JSON

.PP
\fB--timeout\fP=2m0s
	maximum time to wait for operation completion

.PP
\fB--wait\fP[=false]
	wait for the operation to reach a terminal state


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--ephemeral\fP[=false]
	use the temporary preview lifecycle

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  pb tunnel rename web website
  pb tunnel rename tunnel_abc123 web --wait
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-tunnel(1)\fP
